aliases:
  - Joker Worlds
date: 2026-06-08T00:00:00-04:00
---

Most worlds along the [[Infinite Horizon]] are copies of [[Færrin]] as it would have been without people: empty, and much like the world beside them. A Joker World is one that breaks the pattern. No two are alike, and no one has found why they differ. The gods are asked and do not answer.

A Joker World shows a magical presence where the empty worlds show none. Some are wrapped in slip-shielding, and a traveler who tries to slip into one is turned back at its edge.

The first Joker World voidward of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]]'s edge is blanketed in blood rain, under constant heavy winds and torrents. It is one of the milder Joker Worlds. They grow worse the farther they sit from [[Geography/Færrin|Færrin prime]], and a whole different set lies starward. Some span a long stretch of the horizon at once, so a traveller cannot slip past them and must cross them instead.

Naturally occurring magic items are found in Joker Worlds and nowhere else along the crossing; the empty interstitial worlds between them hold no people and no such items. A map of the worlds voidward would tell which Joker Worlds lie ahead and roughly when, though none of the guests admits to holding one.
